// Copilot review (PR #2516), round-2 comment 4113556120: the ORIGINAL
// version of this fixture put a same-named private fn in this module that
// was never called, so the table collision it claimed to pin could never
// have affected `main.sio`'s output either way -- it wasn't a regression
// test. This `make_pair` IS an unrelated PRIVATE fn (never `use`d by
// anyone, unreachable from `main`), under the exact SAME bare name as the
// REAL, SELECTED import in tta_callee.sio -- but with a DIFFERENT
// tuple-array shape/mask (slot 0 here is the f64 array; slot 1 is there).
// Before this review round's fix (module_loader.sio's per-unit collector
// used to hand this whole module's raw item list to the tuple-array
// collector, not just the one export `touch_other` that main.sio's
// `use` actually names), whichever of these two same-named `make_pair`s
// got collected FIRST inside main's unit won the shared bare-name slot in
// LOWER_FN_TUPLE_ARR_* -- `main.sio`'s `use` for THIS module comes first,
// so this one's mask would have been collected before tta_callee's real
// export, and the real export's own (different) mask would then have lost
// the "already present" dedup check entirely.
fn make_pair() -> ([f64; 2], i64) with Mut, Panic, Div, Alloc {
    ([1.0, 2.0], 9)
}

pub fn touch_other() -> i64 {
    99
}
